Subject: Re: [GSoC] Implementing JTAPI

 

Glen,

> Sorry for the late reply.  I have been looking into opinion for this
year's
> GSoc projects.  I am trying to extend the current JTAPI project to allow a
> second student.   We have a strong candidate for the existing JTAPI
project. 
> So what I going to try and propose to have a second JTAPI activity that
> begins the development of JDF job-ticket JTAPI input module.  This means,
a
> module that can read JDF job-ticket, translate it JTAPI object/attributes,
> and then calls the JTAPI.  If time permits it would nice to create the
> output module which does the opposite.   
> 

Thank you for your reply. I will be interested in writing input and output
modules for the JTAPI. Since, you say that it will not require much domain
knowledge, I think I will be able to do a good job since I will not be
spending too much time learning internals.

> I don't believe this will require any unique domain (printing) knowledge. 
> The project is basically a parser, hash (translation) functions and API
> calling. 

Please tell me more about it so that I will be able to make a proper
proposal. Specifically, will these input and output modules constitute
another separate library that applications will make calls to? Is a more
detailed specification available currently? I would like to get a better
feel of the scope and content of the project because I feel that there will
be enough time (in 3 months) to create both the input and the output modules
that you speak of.


Aditya




